⭐ Day 17 in One Sentence

Requests tell Kubernetes how much CPU/memory a container needs for scheduling, while limits define the maximum CPU/memory it is allowed to use.

🔑 Quick Memory Trick
REQUEST → Need → Scheduling

LIMIT   → Maximum → Usage

CPU     → Throttle if limit reached

Memory  → Can be OOMKilled if limit exceeded

